  {
    "type": 19,
    "content": "They were free to remove it; and people are free to recreate it. More than half the data in there was sourced from other people not affiliated with the guide creators; it was made publicly available. Many of the content on the guide was provided by people who have since quit the game long before companions. \n\nThe knights who want to treat this like it's some copyright/plagiarism/ethical/moral issue need to get a grip. They didn't own the majority of the information on that guide; they simply compiled it into one place. It was appreciated, and they could have sent their message without trying to create false outrage by upsetting a plethora of people who relied on the resource. \n\nThey were attempting to get more people mad about pets. It didn't work; and the internet did what the internet do.",
